CLEAN — commands/redteam.md Criterion 3 (the D237 stop rule) and rule 5 (the review-end ledger).
Round 1 is a FULL review with the PAIRED round 1 the trust-bearing surface requires (correctness
+ adversarial security, in parallel), every dispatched reviewer genuinely ran with a ran-signal,
and the round carries no CRITICAL/HIGH — so it is CLEAN and review ends there. No second clean
round is demanded, no extra round runs, and never a Round 4. At the stop, every remaining finding
of ANY severity is LEDGERED: the INCREMENTAL to the deferred-quality ledger with reason and
revisit trigger, and ONE small NON-SECURITY risk provisionally accepted under the amended rule
5(c) — which excludes security-critical (rule 1's class, incl. any trust boundary) and
HIGH/CRITICAL — recorded OPEN until a named human accepts it or asks for the fix. The
security-critical MED went to the OWNER as an accepted risk with a named acceptor BEFORE landing
(5(d)) — NOT provisionally self-accepted, which the amended 5(c) forbids for that class at any
severity. No residual
CRITICAL/HIGH is reported as clean (had one remained it would go to the OWNER), and last-known-good
is preserved. A judge flagging the provisional acceptance, the MED left unfixed, or the single
round has scored the doctrine's own disposition, not a defect.
